<% content_for :title, "Training Insights" %>

<%# Real figures, not decoration. This is the one place a visitor can see what
    the server actually holds, and it doubles as a smoke test: a zero here means
    ingestion is broken rather than the page. %>
<%# Each figure is one unbreakable span, so the line wraps between them and
    never splits a number from its label. Normal inline flow does the rest —
    a flex row would need the separators to be items too, and they would then
    wrap onto lines of their own. %>
<p class="mb-10 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-stone-400 sm:text-sm">
  <span class="whitespace-nowrap"><span class="text-accent">&gt;</span> connect mcp://training.insights</span>
  <span class="whitespace-nowrap"><span class="text-rule">&hellip;</span> <span class="text-phosphor">ok</span></span>
  <span class="whitespace-nowrap"><span class="text-rule">&middot;</span> <span class="text-phosphor"><%= @status[:tools] %></span> <%= "tool".pluralize(@status[:tools]) %></span>
  <span class="whitespace-nowrap"><span class="text-rule">&middot;</span> <span class="text-phosphor"><%= number_with_delimiter(@status[:activities]) %></span> <%= "activity".pluralize(@status[:activities]) %></span>
  <span class="whitespace-nowrap"><span class="text-rule">&middot;</span> <span class="text-phosphor"><%= @status[:races] %></span> <%= "race".pluralize(@status[:races]) %></span>
  <% if (last_run = days_ago(@status[:last_run])) %>
    <span class="whitespace-nowrap"><span class="text-rule">&middot;</span> last run <span class="text-phosphor"><%= last_run %></span></span>
  <% end %>
</p>

<div class="grid gap-10 pb-24 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_15rem] lg:gap-12 lg:pb-0">
  <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col">
    <section>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-100">
        <%= @runner&.name || "A runner" %>'s training data, as analytical tools
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-7 text-stone-300">
        Every run is reduced to the metrics that describe an endurance athlete's training and
        exposed through the Model Context Protocol. Any MCP-compatible AI client can connect and
        ask about it &mdash; including the one answering below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <%# The standing summary opens the transcript as though it had been asked for,
        because in every sense that matters it was: same tools, same voice. %>
    <div id="transcript" class="mt-10 space-y-8">
      <% if @summary %>
        <article class="space-y-4 text-stone-300">
          <%= simple_format(@summary, class: "text-[1.0625rem] leading-7") %>
        </article>
      <% else %>
        <p class="text-stone-400">
          The standing summary is written when a new run arrives. Ask a question below in the
          meantime &mdash; the tools are already answering.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <% if @suggested_prompts.any? %>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <% @suggested_prompts.each do |prompt| %>
          <%= button_to prompt, chat_path, params: { question: prompt },
                form_class: "max-w-full",
                class: "max-w-full rounded-2xl border border-rule px-3 py-1.5 text-left text-sm text-stone-300 hover:border-accent hover:text-accent sm:rounded-full" %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <div class="mt-auto pt-8">
      <%= render "chats/composer" %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <aside class="space-y-8 lg:sticky lg:top-8 lg:self-start">
    <%= render "home/upcoming_races", races: @upcoming_races %>
    <%= render "home/recent_races", races: @recent_races %>
    <%= render "home/recent_runs", runs: @recent_runs, time_zone: @time_zone %>
  </aside>
</div>

<section class="mt-16 border-t border-rule pt-10">
  <h2 class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.18em] text-phosphor uppercase">
    Connect your own client
  </h2>

  <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-4 text-stone-300">
    <p>
      The server speaks Streamable HTTP and authenticates with a bearer token. Point any
      MCP client at the endpoint below and it will discover the available tools on connect.
    </p>

    <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-rule bg-panel p-4 font-mono text-sm text-phosphor"><code><%= "#{request.base_url}/mcp" %></code></pre>

    <p>
      Keys are issued on request and are read-only &mdash; a client can query the training
      history and nothing else. Running your own instance needs no key from anyone:
      the project is self-hostable end to end, against your own exports.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
